 "check": {
  "describe": "Pinned clock 2026-10-30 15:00. Top card ('Temperature'): 24 hourly temperatures as an amber monotone curve over a light amber wash, grid lines at 20/15/10/5° lined up with the labels in the column on the left, hours 0h 6h 12h 18h 23h centred under their x, dots on the low (7.8° at 5 h) and the high (19.4° at 15 h); the header reads 7.8° – 19.4° from the array. Bottom card: the tide fn 1.6 + 1.2·cos((u − 312)·0.0084315) over 00..24 h fills the rest of the height: high water 2.8 m at 05:12 and 17:37, low 0.4 m at 11:25 and 23:50, each with a small dot (the fifth mark, 312 − 372.6, is before midnight and not drawn); a grey vertical line at 15:00 with a large dot on the rising curve at 1.9 m, which the header's '1.9 m now' matches. dark: the same on the dark palette; mono / mono-inverted: no wash, white (black) 2 dp lines and dots, grey grid. narrow (234) and wide (540): the plots and the x labels follow the width, the y labels keep their 32 dp column. shifted (tideHigh 600, a cooling day): high water moves to 10:00 and 22:25 and low water to 03:47 and 16:13, all four dotted (the marks list has five times; the ones outside 00..24 h are not drawn); the now dot sits on the falling side at 0.6 m, as the header says; the temperature curve falls from 19° to 6° with the extremes dotted at its ends and the header reads 6.0° – 19.0°.",
